   "title": "Data Normalization and Standardization",
   "raw": "Data Normalization and Standardization\n\n Min-Max Normalization                                           Z-Score Standardization\n\n Scales values to a fixed range, typically 0 to 1                Centers data with mean=0 and std=1\n\n\n\n  x_norm = (x - min) / (max - min)                                z = (x - mean) / std\n\n\n Use when: Bounded range needed, no extreme outliers             Use when: Comparing across features, algorithms need it\n\n\n\n\n Why Normalize?\n Many ML algorithms (like neural networks, KNN, SVM) are sensitive to feature scales. Without normalization, features with\n larger ranges dominate the model unfairly.\n\n\n Tip: Know when to use each method. This concept appears frequently in ML courses and interviews.\n                                                                                                                             38",
