   "title": "Understanding Distributions",
   "raw": "Understanding Distributions\n\n\n\n\n    Normal (Bell Curve)                     Right-Skewed                         Left-Skewed\n\n     Symmetric around mean.                 Long tail to the right.             Long tail to the left.\n         Mean ≈ median.                      Mean > median.                      Mean < median.\n    Example: Heights, test scores       Example: Income, home prices         Example: Age at retirement\n\n\n\n\n Why it matters: The shape of your distribution determines which statistics and methods are appropriate.\n Skewed data often needs median over mean.\n                                                                                                           43",
