   "title": "Correlation: Measuring Relationships",
   "raw": "Correlation: Measuring Relationships\n\n Correlation is a statistical measure that quantifies the strength and direction of the linear relationship between two\n variables. It ranges from -1 to +1, where -1 indicates perfect negative correlation, 0 indicates no correlation, and +1 indicates\n perfect positive correlation. Ranges from -1 (perfect negative) to +1 (perfect positive).\n\n\n\n\n                +1                                              0                                           -1\n       Positive Correlation                             No Correlation                            Negative Correlation\n\n As X increases, Y increases. More study      No linear relationship. Shoe size → GPA          As X increases, Y decreases. More\n        hours → higher grades                               (hopefully!)                           partying → lower grades\n\n\n\n\n ⚠ CRITICAL: Correlation ≠ Causation. Ice cream sales and drowning deaths are correlated, but ice cream doesn't cause drowning!\n\n\n                                                                                                                                     44",
