   "title": "AI Limitations: What Can Go Wrong?",
   "raw": "AI Limitations: What Can Go Wrong?\n\n  Critical: Understanding these limitations is essential for using AI responsibly and eﬀectively.\n\n\n\n\n HALLUCINATIONS                                                         MATH ERRORS\n AI can generate confident-sounding but completely false information,   LLMs predict words, not compute math. They can make arithmetic\n including fake citations and invented facts.                           and calculation mistakes.\n\n\n OUTDATED KNOWLEDGE                                                     BIAS & STEREOTYPES\n Training data has a cutoff date. AI may not know recent events,        AI can reflect biases from training data, including gender, racial, and\n updated APIs, or new research.                                         cultural stereotypes.\n\n\n\n\nThe rule: Always verify AI outputs. Trust but verify — especially for facts, calculations, and code.                                              54",
