   "raw": "Data Science-Specific Prompts\nDifferent tasks require different prompting patterns. Here are templates you'll use throughout this course.\n\n\n\n\n FOR CODE                                                                      FOR ANALYSIS\n Specify language, libraries, input/output formats, and error handling         Describe data structure, analysis goal, and what insights you're looking\n requirements.\n   \"Write Python code using pandas to... Input is CSV with columns...          for.\n                                                                                 \"I have a dataset with [columns]. I want to understand [goal]. Suggest\n  Return a DataFrame with...\"                                                   approaches to…\"\n\n\n FOR DEBUGGING                                                                 FOR EXPLANATION\n Include error message, what you've tried, and expected vs. actual behavior.   State your current understanding level and what specifically confuses you.\n\n  \"I get this error: [error]. I expected [X] but got [Y]. I've already tried    \"I understand [A] but I'm confused about [B]. Can you explain with a\n  [Z]…\"                                                                         concrete example?\"\n\n\n\n\nThese patterns will be your daily tools. Save them and adapt them to your specific needs.                                                                   57",
