   "title": "Summary: Foundation Models",
   "raw": "Summary: Foundation Models\n\n Foundation models are powerful learning partners\n Pre-trained on massive data, they can explain, code, analyze, and debug — but you must verify their outputs.\n\n\n\n Prompt engineering is a learnable skill\n Be specific, provide context, iterate, and verify. Use techniques like chain-of-thought, role prompting, and structured output.\n\n\n\n AI has real limitations you must understand\n Hallucinations, outdated knowledge, math errors, and bias. Trust but always verify using the VERIFY framework.\n\n\n\n Responsible use is non-negotiable\n Use AI to learn and understand — never as a shortcut. Be transparent about AI assistance. You own your work.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                                   63",
